Ques15: Activity:- Identify and Label the Components of a Drone
Components and their Functions:
Flight Controller – Controls and stabilizes the drone.
ESC (Electronic Speed Controller) – Controls the speed of the motors.
BLDC Motors – Rotate the propellers.
Propellers – Generate lift and thrust.
Li-Po Battery – Supplies power to the drone.
GPS Module – Provides location and navigation.
Radio Receiver – Receives signals from the remote controller.
Frame – Holds all the drone components together.
Camera – Captures photos and videos.
Telemetry Module – Sends flight data to the ground station.
Observations: All these components work together to help the drone take off, hover, move, navigate, and land safely.
